Subject: Cantor Temporal Planner Support Slice 04 Proof and Downstream Handoff

Description: Integrated proof, release audit, and separately governed Operator Shell handoff cluster.

@ [slice_file_id] FSS-CTPR-004_proof_and_downstream_handoff
@ [slice_file_uuid] 72c6e70f-bcf3-4641-aee1-e2c8b62972e7
@ [support_slice_index] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\cantor_temporal_planner_development\index.sop

& [ClusterIdentity] is integration and handoff
  + [enqueue_readiness] is WS-CTPR-014_ready_WS-CTPR-015_and_016_blocked
  + [reason_for_contiguity] is integrated replay proves the runtime, release audit establishes support, and only then may Operator Shell consume the profile

& [FeatureRequirementSet] is atomic
  + [feature_requirement] is FR-CTPR-014
    @ [support_status] ready
    + [requirement_statement] is prove the logical-time three-step walk, deliberate deviation, rear refusal, invalidation, replan, dual-pass compiler review, and deterministic replay
  + [feature_requirement] is FR-CTPR-015
    @ [support_status] blocked
    + [requirement_statement] is audit requirements, negative proofs, test results, support and requirement deltas, authority scope, and release readiness
  + [feature_requirement] is FR-CTPR-016
    @ [support_status] blocked
    + [requirement_statement] is provide a read-only E0/E1 temporal-planning handoff to the separately governed Operator Shell without enabling live calendar or desktop effects

& [WorkSliceTransform] is the proof and handoff queue
  + [work_slice_detail] is WS-CTPR-014
    @ [slice_status] ready_unassigned
    @ [model_routing] Spark-suitable for closed fixture integration after component proofs
    @ [depends_on] WS-CTPR-011, WS-CTPR-012, and WS-CTPR-013
    + [scope] is integrated deterministic first proof and negative suite
    + [completion_criteria] is normalized replay and every CTPR negative proof pass without live effects
  + [work_slice_detail] is WS-CTPR-015
    @ [slice_status] blocked
    @ [model_routing] Spark-suitable for evidence collation; premium review required for authority conclusion
    @ [depends_on] WS-CTPR-014
    + [scope] is release audit, requirement accounting, support review, residuals, and rollback
    + [completion_criteria] is truthful verified, partial, failed, deferred, and superseded accounting
  + [work_slice_detail] is WS-CTPR-016
    @ [slice_status] blocked
    @ [model_routing] Requires premium model
    @ [depends_on] WS-CTPR-015 and COS-SJS-01
    + [scope] is Operator Shell consumption contract over read-only temporal proposal and reentry surfaces
    + [completion_criteria] is E0/E1 integration preserves privacy, consent, capability, and no-live-effect boundaries

& [SupportGapSet] is explicit
  + [support_gap] is SG-CTPR-014
    @ [gap_status] resolved_for_WS-CTPR-014
    @ [blocks] WS-CTPR-015_until_integrated_proof
    + [historical_gap_statement] is component runtime implementation and proof were absent
    + [resolution] is WS-CTPR-011 through WS-CTPR-013 completed with focused proofs and completed-work reviews
  + [support_gap] is SG-CTPR-016
    @ [blocks] WS-CTPR-016
    + [gap_statement] is COS-SJS-01 and CTPR release evidence are both absent
